ity and Budget Management Act-2003, the Indian government shall not borrow from the ______ except by way of advances to meet temporary excess of cash disbursements over cash receipts.</span></p>","option_1":"State Bank of India","option_2":"Reserve Bank of India","option_3":"National Bank for Rural Development","option_4":"Small Industries Development Bank of India","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"2","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option B - Reserve Bank of India.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>The FRBM Act, 2003 restricts the central government from borrowing directly from the Reserve Bank of India, except through Ways and Means Advances (WMA) to cover temporary mismatches between cash receipts and disbursements, in order to curb automatic monetisation of the deficit.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"31386","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"844","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":"<style> *{overflow-wrap: break-word;} </style> <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>As per data of Ministry of Mines, production of iron ore was ______ million metric tonnes (MMT)